WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.535
-Our next guest has his
new stand-up special

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.705
"Born in '86" available now
on YouTube.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.140
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.309
please welcome the very funny
D.J. Demers.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:12.178
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:18.918
♪♪

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.886
-Hello.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.987
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.055
How are ya?

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:24.624
Thank you, thank you so much.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.759
What a dream.
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.562
Keep that applause going for my
interpreter Caroline, everybody.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.199
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.301
Yeah.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.136
Yeah, I wanted to have
an interpreter.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:39.605
I wanted to make sure
that all my deaf homies

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.642
could appreciate the show
as well, 'cause I'm deaf.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.478
You know, I'm not full deaf.
I wear hearing aids.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.413
I actually don't know
sign language myself.

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.115
I'm bad at being deaf,

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.517
But --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.585
Yeah, I'm not good
at hearing either.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.621
I'm like a daywalker.
I don't --

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.021
I don't know where I belong.

00:00:56.021 --> 00:00:59.025
But I actually learned recently
there's a bit of a beef

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.694
between the deaf and
hard-of-hearing communities --

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.530
a quiet beef,
but a --

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.831
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.801
But a -- But a beef nonetheless.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.368
But I want no part of that.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.771
I got nothing but love
for everybody, deaf people.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:15.074
I've never felt deafer
than I did during this pandemic.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.209
For real, man.
Everybody's had a mask on.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.211
I haven't had a real
conversation in two years.

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:20.613
I don't know --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.681
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.083
Honestly. For real.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:27.020
Gosh, it's been brutal.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.488
People used to always ask me,
like,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.223
"How much can you actually hear
and how much are you, like,

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.958
lip-reading?" and now that
everybody's been covering

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:35.394
their mouth, I was finally able
to run the numbers,

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:40.233
and it turned out I'm
lip-reading 100% of the time.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.134
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.736
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.371
Man, oh, man.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.973
The worst is when they have
a mask on

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.208
and they're behind plexiglass,
you know?

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.910
You walk into the bank,
you're looking at a guy.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.712
He's got the mask on.
He's behind the glass.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.247
I just -- I'm staring at the
teller for like 10 seconds

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:57.149
before I'm finally just like,
"Hey, man,

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.184
have you started talking yet?"

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.219
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.055
"I legitimately have no idea."

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.155
[ Applause ]

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.224
Man, if this is important,

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.859
could you --
If this is important,

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.228
could you, like, write it
on a piece of paper

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.529
and put it up against the glass,

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.532
like a reverse robbery
situation?

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.266
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:15.535
Man.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.869
I don't know sign language,

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.772
but I realize that it might be
time for me to learn.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.773
You know?

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.209
But that wasn't learned,
by the way.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.043
That was poop.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.578
But --

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.046
That was a joke
for my deaf homies.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.914
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.683
Might have ruined the joke
by explaining it,

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.418
but I had to
for my blind homies.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.054
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.524
Yeah. Had to do it.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.958
Yeah.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.793
I knew the pandemic was real
when they took

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.029
all the sports away.
That's when I knew.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.330
You know, 'cause I'm an idiot.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.464
Like, when I first
started hearing about COVID,

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:46.866
I was one of those morons.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.601
I was like, "Guys, this'll
be over in four or five days.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.902
We'll be back to business."

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.237
And then they took
all the sports away.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.772
I was like,
"It's pretty serious, guys.

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:55.541
Pretty serious.
They took all the sports away.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:59.078
We should probably start washing
our hands."

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.547
They took them all away,
and I love sports.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:02.948
Like, I need sports.

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:04.316
When they took them away --
Like, I love every sport --

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:05.785
violent sports.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.886
I mean, it is a bit difficult
for me to watch violent sports

00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:09.888
sometimes because I played
a lot of hockey growing up

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:11.357
and I got a lot of concussions,

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.693
and I feel like they might have
scrambled my brain a little bit,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.228
but I don't know,
I just love violent sports.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:18.631
It is a little hard for me to
watch violent sports sometimes,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.399
though, 'cause I played a lot
of hockey growing up

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.368
and I got a lot of concussions

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.336
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.937
And...

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:27.440
[ Applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.411
Feel like I might have scrambled
my brain a little bit, but...

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.811
That but was a joke,
but if I do it again,

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:33.980
call an ambulance, please.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.983
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.317
But, yeah, then they took them
all away.

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:39.919
All of a sudden, I had no sports
to watch.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.554
I had to, like --
I went on YouTube.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.989
I started watching weird,
random sports

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:45.725
just to fill the void
in my heart.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.125
I got into darts for a while.

00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:48.327
I was watching darts.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.129
Cornhole --
I got deep into cornhole.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.530
That was weird.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.665
I started watching a lot
of speed walking.

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:55.467
Speed walking is amazing,
though.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:56.569
Like, I stand by that.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.870
I know it's easy to hate
on speed walking.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.840
I've been there, but once
you get over your prejudice,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.943
undeniably the sexiest sport
on the planet.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.778
You know? Undenia--

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.314
What other sport is literally
all in the hips?

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.982
You know?
And they go hard.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:13.185
They go for 50 kilometers --
31 miles.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:16.255
30-- Could you imagine doing
this for 31 miles?

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:18.090
[ Grunting ]

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:22.395
[ Applause ]
My hips would break.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.430
Man, it's no joke.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.964
You know what I love
about speed walking, too?

00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:28.000
It's the only sport with, like,
a built-in limit.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.003
Every other sport, the coaches
are like, "Give it 110%."

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:32.404
Speed walking is the only one
where they're like,

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:35.241
"Better cap it at 98%,"
you know?

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.276
"If we're not careful,
this could turn into a jog."

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:41.714
It's a dangerous game
we're playing here.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:43.382
Speed walking's got
a marketing problem.

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.418
It should be
the biggest sport on the planet.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.420
What I would do if I was
in charge of speed walking,

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.989
I would license it out
to all the other sports,

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.391
and create brand-new beautiful
sports with speed walking.

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.626
Take your favorite sport,

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.394
add speed walking
to the front of it,

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:57.296
you got a beautiful --
Think of any sport you want.

00:04:57.296 --> 00:04:58.631
Speed walking baseball.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.400
You see it?

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.668
You see it, right?

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:05.104
A guy up to bat, just hits
the it to the left field,

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.072
guy is going down
to first base.

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:08.507
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:11.677
Outfielder trying
to track it down.

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:14.013
Come on.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.281
Speed walking football.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.448
Could you imagine
speed walking --

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:17.850
Just, hut!

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.184
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:21.654
Receiver trying to get it.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.989
Come on.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:26.725
Man, oh, man. It doesn't even
have to be, like, a real sport.

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:28.594
Like, a random event
I would watch

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.196
if they added speed walking
to it.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.764
You know the running
with the bulls they do

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.332
every year in Spain?

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:34.433
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.735
Big deal.
Anybody can run with the bulls.

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:39.505
Let's see what you're really
made out of, you know?

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:40.940
Speed walking with the bulls.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.076
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.777
Thousands of people die
every year.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.111
What a sport.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:48.547
Pure violence.

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:50.049
Be a little hard for me
to watch, though,

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.817
because I played a lot of hockey
growing up

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:54.320
and I got a lot of --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.189
What's so funny?

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.156
You guys have been amazing.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.190
Thank you so much.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.626
I'm D.J.
Caroline, everybody.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:03.396
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, come on!

00:06:05.163 --> 00:06:07.099
Oh, my God, fantastic.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:09.235
D.J. Demers right there.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.404
"Born in '86"...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:14.673
...is available now on YouTube.

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:16.542
We'll be right back, everybody.
Come on back.

